From: mosdns v2 rebuild
Subject: [PATCH] fence cache entries and dumps across successful rule reloads

Keep live rule replacement, but serialize successful publication with cache
access and reject results started under an earlier generation. Flush every
cache and invalidate persistent dumps on publication. Normal, lazy and
prefetch work all retain their original generation.

Startup dump provenance remains the service launcher responsibility; legacy
dumps are accepted only before the first live publication in this process.

